  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Friday)\nIssued at 1222 PM CDT SAT SEP 26 2026\n\nWe were treated to another cool start this morning with temps\ngenerally in the mid 50s to low 60s. Water vapor imagery reveals\nan upper level ridge continuing to progress each into the region\nas a nor'easter moves just off the east coast. This upper level\nridge and surface high pressure will help maintain pleasant\nconditions in place across Central Alabama with highs in the low\nto mid 80s, lows in the mid 50s to low 60s, and rain-free\nconditions.\n\nThe upper level pattern begins to change early next week as a\nweak shortwave cuts into the Tennessee Valley on Monday and\nTuesday, followed by a stronger upper trough late in the work\nweek. However, limited moisture in place keeps dry conditions in\nplace through mid week. Low to medium chances for showers and\nstorms return to the forecast late in the week as the\naforementioned upper trough and accompanying cold front near the\nregion.\n\nA more southerly flow returns by early next week which will\nunfortunately lead to warming temperatures across Central\nAlabama. High temps rebound into the upper 80s to 90 degrees by\nTuesday and look to continue through the work week.\n\n95/Castillo",
